Package: mos-mqttd
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: mos build <mos@example.invalid>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: mosd (= @VERSION@), passwd, ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: mos D-Bus to MQTT application bridge
 Publishes the item trees of explicitly enrolled applications onto an MQTT
 broker, and carries write topics back to SetValue only when it is started in
 full mode. It owns /usr/lib/mos/mqtt-applications.d, the enrollment directory
 application packages drop their names into.
 .
 The dependency on mosd is pinned to the exact version because mosd renders
 this bridge's runtime configuration into /run and owns its lifecycle, and the
 two are built from one workspace commit across an interface that carries no
 compatibility promise.
 .
 There is no dependency on mos-mqtt-broker. The bridge reads the broker's
 address from STATE and may be pointed at one that is not on this device,
 which is why the two are separate packages.
 .
 passwd is needed by the postinst, which creates the pinned mos-mqttd service
 account with useradd, groupadd and chage. dpkg-shlibdeps cannot see a program
 that is exec'd by name, so that dependency is written out here.
 .
 The unit ships DISABLED: no multi-user.target.wants symlink is in this
 payload and nothing enables it. mosd starts and stops the bridge from the
 mqtt settings subtree.
